## What to deliver

Build and rig the walker up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png` matches
the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together correctly,
and the rig is complete: a squat armored body carried on legs, a turret up on its back,
and twin flak barrels raked toward the sky. **Author the two required animations** as
F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `walk` (a walk whose feet plant
flat and still, then lift and swing — with weight, not a weightless slide) and
`flak_track` (the turret traversing and the barrels elevating to track a target while
the walker stands its ground). The animations are the fixed contract — produce both, by
those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When you are satisfied,
stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
